\par\b\fs28 \u167?4 Sources round\b0\fs24\par


\par Van de Giessen now covers Deuteronomy (18\u8211?34); the rabbinic witnesses were verified via Sefaria.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Van de Giessen (pre-peshat).\b0  Tsur (Rock) is the Godname of this song \u8212? as refuge/protection \u8212? recurring in 32:4, 15, 18, 30, while the idols are precisely no rock (32:31, 37). Jeshurun (32:15) is the symbolic ideal-name for Israel; the verb ba'at (32:15, \u8220?to kick / to spurn\u8221?) occurs only here and in 1 Sam. 2:29. In 32:18 shayah (\u8220?to neglect / forget\u8221?) is a hapax, and the Rock \u8220?begets and bears\u8221? \u8212? paternal and maternal language for God being Israel's origin. The song is marked in the text itself by setumot and column layout; DSS witnesses (4QDeut) generally follow MT.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Rashi on 32:1 (Sifrei Devarim 306).\b0  Heaven and earth are called as witnesses because they endure forever: Moses is mortal and dies tomorrow; so Israel cannot later say \u8220?we never accepted the covenant.\u8221? Second reason: the same witnesses reward or punish \u8212? the vine yields fruit, the ground its increase, the heaven its dew \u8212? or withhold it. That dew note already anchors the image of 32:2 (and Hosea 14) at the peshat.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Two witnesses (Deut. 19:15).\b0  Heaven and earth form the pair of witnesses the Torah requires \u8212? a legal, not a decorative, move.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8223? \b Midrash Tanchuma (Ha'azinu 2).\b0  Moses says ha'azinu to heaven and \u8220?hear\u8221? to earth; Isaiah 1:2 reverses the order \u8212? the speaker's nearness colours the address. Illustrative, not load-bearing.\par


\par \u9898? \b Onkelos / Ibn Ezra / Ramban\b0  on 32:4/32:15: still to be verified (open verification point).\par


\par \b Revision gate.\b0  Did the round shift the centre? Confirming: Rashi's dew note and Van de Giessen's tsur-concentration strengthen Source+Trajectory and the dew-echo to Hosea, without collapsing it to Source alone.\par



\par\b\fs28 \u167?5 Direction test as horizon\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? Confessional. Matthew 18:21\u8211?35 continues Ha'azinu's forgetting-line from the other side: the servant forgiven an immeasurable debt who seizes his fellow by the throat is Jeshurun who forgot the Rock \u8212? the forgetting becomes visible in the hard hand. \u8220?From Me is your fruit found\u8221? (Hos.): the fruit of received grace is grace passed on. \u-10179?\u-8908? Guarded: Matt. 18 does not determine the peshat of Deut. 32; it is horizon. And \u8220?seventy times seven\u8221? is no new counting but the end of counting \u8212? as the Rock stops counting against the one who returns.\par



